{
 "description": "SQL worksheet (Admin): SQL run against an Oracle database from this PC, as in SQL Developer. Connections (Basic: host, port, SID or service name; TNS: an alias of tnsnames.ora; or a connect identifier) are kept by the desktop app on this PC, passwords in the OS keychain; Test, Save and Connect as in SQL Developer's New / Select Database Connection. Ctrl+Enter runs the statement under the cursor, F5 the script; results in a grid with fetch more; changes wait for Commit or Rollback; DBMS output, history and export. The desktop app runs it (desktop/lib/oracleSql.js, node-oracledb Thin); not available in VBCS. Ask AI: a question in plain words, and the LLM chosen in its settings (Claude, ChatGPT, Oracle OCI Generative AI, Gemini or any OpenAI-compatible service, with the person's own key kept encrypted by the desktop app) writes the SQL into the worksheet, selected, never run by itself; it is sent the question and the names of the tables and columns, never rows.",
 "navigation": {
  "embeddable": "enabled"
 },
